# common.list — official-repo (pacman) packages, real Arch names, one per line.
# AUR packages live in aur.list. GPU/Vulkan drivers are installed per-vendor by
# phase 40, not here. Comments (#) and blank lines are ignored.

# ── core session ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
hyprland
quickshell
hypridle
hyprlock
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
polkit
gnome-keyring
libsecret               # secret-tool — Google refresh token lives in the keyring
# kdeconnect: NOT here since 0.44 — the Phone plugin (ewe.phone) `requires` it and Komble
# installs it with the plugin; it pulled ~165 MB of KDE Frameworks into every install.
accountsservice         # user icon store (greeter avatar; Settings writes it via busctl)
plocate                 # launcher file search (Super+D); phase 30 enables the updatedb timer
python-dbus             # logind-bridge.py, bt-agent.py and the phone add-on's kdeconnect-bridge.py (D-Bus side)
python-gobject          # those two bridges' GLib loop (also the optional EDS helper)
openssh                 # ssh + a per-user sshd: Remote (RFC-009, ewe-remote) and the SSH plugin
python-spake2           # Remote pairing: the 8-digit code is checked with SPAKE2 (no offline guessing)
qt6-wayland
qt6-svg
qt6-5compat
qt6-multimedia-ffmpeg
xdg-user-dirs
xdg-utils

# ── greeter / welcome screen — FULLY WAYLAND, zero Xorg. greetd is the login
#    daemon; ReGreet (gtk4-layer-shell, Wayland-native) is the graphical greeter,
#    rendered by `cage` (a one-shot kiosk Wayland compositor). All three are in
#    the official extra repo. No xorg-server anywhere. ──────────────────────────
greetd
greetd-regreet
cage
plymouth                # graphical boot splash (Arch logo + spinner); wired by phase 35

# ── audio (PipeWire, low-latency-ready) ──────────────────────────────────────
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack
pipewire-audio          # SPA codec/bluetooth plugins — BT speakers/headsets expose a sink
wireplumber
pavucontrol
# Audio FIRMWARE — modern Intel (Lunar Lake / Arc) and recent AMD laptops route
# audio through the on-die SOF DSP; without sof-firmware the codec never loads and
# there is NO sound on real hardware (a VM's virtio audio needs no firmware, which
# is exactly why it works in a VM but is silent on metal).
sof-firmware
alsa-ucm-conf           # UCM routing profiles (speakers / headphone jack / mic)
alsa-utils              # alsactl (restore mixer @ boot) + alsamixer / aplay -l diagnostics

# ── network / bluetooth / power ──────────────────────────────────────────────
networkmanager
networkmanager-openvpn  # OpenVPN profiles (the most common VPN type)
networkmanager-l2tp     # L2TP/IPsec profiles (server + user + password + PSK — the corporate/ISP kind); xl2tpd rides along.
                        # The IPsec half is libreswan (aur.list), NOT strongswan: strongSwan 6.1 (Arch, 2026-09)
                        # dropped IKEv1 at build time and L2TP/IPsec is IKEv1-only — every profile died with
                        # "The VPN service failed to start" (charon: "IKE version 1 not supported").
tailscale               # built in, set up from ewe: installed everywhere, but tailscaled is NOT enabled by
                        # any phase — Quick settings → Wi-Fi → "Set up Tailscale" runs `ewe-tailscale setup`
                        # (one pkexec: enable --now tailscaled + `tailscale set --operator=<you>`), so the
                        # daemon only runs for someone who asked for it
ethtool                 # read-only: the NIC's supported link modes, so Quick settings can say "Cable runs at
                        # 100 Mb/s — the cable or port may be faulty" only when the port can do 1 Gb/s or more
# Cast to TV (the ewe.cast add-on's "Cast" tile → gnome-network-displays, aur.list; deps stay here, D7):
iw                      # `iw list` — the add-on's cast-check.sh verifies the Wi-Fi card does Wi-Fi Direct (P2P), which Miracast needs
avahi                   # mDNS — Chromecast / Google TV discovery (phase 30 enables avahi-daemon)
wireless-regdb          # regulatory database; phase 30 sets the country. Without it the kernel runs the
                        # "world" domain: 5 GHz is receive-only, so hotspot / Wi-Fi Direct (Miracast) are
                        # pinned to crowded 2.4 GHz — the "laggy / frozen mirror" of 2026-08-21
gst-plugin-va           # VA-API in GStreamer: hardware DECODING for ewe Player / ewe Viewer video, and
                        # vah264enc — hardware H.264 for Cast to TV (gnome-network-displays prefers it over
                        # x264); Intel iHD + AMD Mesa both expose it via VA-API
gst-plugins-bad         # fdkaacenc / faac — the AAC encoders Cast to TV needs for the audio half of the
                        # stream. Without one the daemon casts video only; it used to route the user's
                        # audio into a null sink it could not read back, so casting silenced the machine.
                        # Pulled in transitively on most desktops; an ISO cannot rely on "most".
bluez
bluez-utils
blueman
power-profiles-daemon
upower                  # battery/AC state for the bar, control centre and display re-asserts
fwupd                   # firmware/BIOS updates from Linux (LVFS) — stale vendor BIOS is the
                        # root cause behind ACPI poweroff/suspend bugs on thin laptops

# ── terminal (single, fast, GPU-accelerated) ─────────────────────────────────
# kitty is the one terminal (foot/ghostty dropped). No multiplexer: Hyprland
# already does windows/workspaces. kitty launches zsh (dotfiles/kitty/
# ewe-shell.sh); the LOGIN shell stays bash.
kitty

# ── terminal shell: zsh + plugins (all official repos) ──────────────────────
# The interactive shell is zsh with its plugins, the fuzzy finder, modern ls/
# cat, and the system-info fetch — all from the OFFICIAL repos so they arrive on
# BOTH install paths (install.sh AND the pacman `ewe` package, whose depends are
# generated from this list). The prompt stays oh-my-posh (packages/aur.list),
# wired into ~/.zshrc / ~/.bashrc by dotfiles/shell/shell-setup.sh. fzf/bat also
# appear in dev.list (--dev); the duplicate is harmless (pacman --needed skips).
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions      # fish-style inline suggestions as you type
zsh-syntax-highlighting  # colour commands as you type (sourced LAST, per its docs)
zsh-completions          # extra completion functions (installed into site-functions)
zsh-history-substring-search  # up/down search the history by prefix
fzf                      # Ctrl-R history / Ctrl-T files / Alt-C cd
bash-completion          # programmable completion for bash
eza                      # modern ls (aliased only when present)
bat                      # syntax-highlighting cat/pager (not aliased — cat stays cat)
zoxide                   # smarter cd that remembers where you go
fastfetch                # the neofetch replacement (neofetch is gone from the repos)

# ── files, media and documents = ewe's own apps (0.44) ───────────────────────
#    ewe Files (folders + archives), ewe Player (video + music) and ewe Viewer
#    (PDF, books, documents, pictures) come in the `ewe-apps` package from the
#    [ewe] repo (a dependency of the ewe package, see packaging/PKGBUILD) — the
#    ewe Browser look, the design-system tokens, nothing resident. They replaced
#    Nemo, Engrampa, imv, Zathura (+ mupdf/tesseract) and mpv as the defaults
#    (2026-11-19). mpv itself stays installed: mpvpaper (aur.list) links libmpv.
#    Defaults stay the standard way: ONE ~/.config/mimeapps.list, read natively
#    by GIO (packaging/ewe-setup, phase 60). ─────────────────────────────────────
# Codecs. ewe Player and ewe Viewer play through WebKitGTK → GStreamer: base +
# good (containers, VP8/9, FLAC, Opus…), bad (AV1, HEVC via libde265, DTS, AAC),
# ugly (MPEG-2, AC-3, MP3 encoders), libav (FFmpeg — WMV/WMA, DivX/Xvid, ALAC,
# APE, and everything else; without it a lot of real-world video says "no
# decoder"), va (hardware decoding on Intel/AMD through VA-API).
gst-plugins-base
gst-plugins-good
gst-plugins-ugly
gst-libav
ffmpeg                  # ffprobe/ffmpeg: video thumbnails, stream info, the screenshot of a frame
libdvdcss               # reads encrypted (CSS) DVDs — gst-plugins-ugly's dvdread opens the disc, this
                        # unlocks it; without it a bought film DVD shows nothing (50 KB)
webp-pixbuf-loader      # WebP in GTK3 apps (blueman, pavucontrol's dialogs, file pickers' previews…):
                        # gdk-pixbuf has no WebP loader of its own, so those apps showed a broken image
guvcview                # camera app (photos + video) — tiny traditional GTK,
                        # the cheese-shaped hole in the default set
galculator              # calculator (GTK3, menubar — follows adw-gtk3 + accent)
mate-system-monitor     # task manager / resources (GTK3, menubar, no headerbar)
ffmpegthumbnailer       # video thumbnails in ewe Files (and the freedesktop cache other apps share)
# mounting + filesystem access (trash, network, MTP) — ewe Files goes through GIO
gvfs
gvfs-mtp
gvfs-smb
rclone                  # ~/Nextcloud (ewe-files) and ~/Google Drive (ewe-drive) mounts
fuse3                   # rclone mount's engine
udisks2
unzip
7zip                     # provides 7z (p7zip was dropped from the Arch repos)
unarchiver               # unar/lsar — RAR for ewe Files (Arch's 7zip has no RAR codec; LGPL, not unrar's licence)
xdg-terminal-exec        # GIO runs Terminal=true apps through it: "Open With → micro" failed with "no terminal" (kitty is the one found)

# ── browser + editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zed (official repo) is THE editor/IDE — GUI, default handler for every text
# mime, themed by colorscheme.sh (~/.config/zed/themes/ewe.json). micro covers
# $EDITOR in a TTY (git commit, visudo, ssh) — a GUI editor can't. neovim/vim
# stay dropped.
# (browser: ewe browser — a first-party app like Komble, served from [ewe] and a
# dependency of the ewe package; Helium left the lists when it replaced it)
zed
micro

# ── desktop utilities ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
swaybg
awww       # swww's Arch package name — animated GIF wallpapers + transitions
gpu-screen-recorder   # GPU-encoded capture + replay buffer — moved here from the AUR
grim
slurp
satty
cliphist
imagemagick             # `ewe-theme scheme from-wallpaper` reads the wallpaper's colours through magick
wtype                   # virtual-keyboard typing — the fill picker (ewe-pass) types logins into the focused window
wl-clipboard
hyprpicker
brightnessctl
playerctl
libnotify                # notify-send — used by the low-battery watcher (Battery.qml)
jq
socat

# ── theming (GTK primary) + fonts ────────────────────────────────────────────
adw-gtk-theme
gnome-themes-extra
# GTK is the primary toolkit now, so theming flows through adw-gtk3 + gsettings.
# qt6ct just gives a dark Fusion palette to any stray Qt app you install (the shell
# itself is Quickshell/Qt but themed by Theme.qml). No more plasma-integration / kde
# platform theme — we ship no KDE apps.
qt6ct
librsvg                  # rsvg-convert — builds the Mocu cursor (phase 20 source step)
xorg-xcursorgen          # xcursorgen — builds the Mocu cursor
xmlstarlet               # cursor hotspot extraction for the Mocu build
noto-fonts               # includes Noto Sans Georgian — the Georgian fallback of both
                         # design-system stacks (Geist and Geist Mono have no Georgian)
noto-fonts-emoji
adobe-source-han-sans-otc-fonts  # Chinese, Japanese and Korean (2026-11-08: no CJK font
                         # shipped, so those scripts drew as boxes everywhere). The
                         # same design as Noto Sans CJK at 112 MB instead of 299 MB
                         # (no serif); fontconfig picks the right regional variant
                         # (dotfiles/fontconfig/fonts.conf)
ttf-nerd-fonts-symbols-mono  # Nerd glyphs for the prompt, now that kitty sets Geist Mono
# The DE faces, Geist and Geist Mono (OFL), are NOT in the Arch repos: the
# variable fonts ship in dotfiles/quickshell/fonts/geist/ and dotfiles/fontconfig
# adds that folder to the font path.
sound-theme-freedesktop  # event chimes (notifications, volume, shutter) — Globals.playSound
ttf-ubuntu-font-family  # the pre-2026-09 DE face; kept installed for now so documents
                        # and configs that still name Ubuntu keep rendering

# ── spell checking ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# enchant (already pulled in by WebKitGTK) finds hunspell dictionaries in
# /usr/share/hunspell; with none installed nothing could check spelling. US
# English ships everywhere; other languages are installed ON DEMAND from
# Settings → Language → Spell checking (hunspell-de, -ru, -fr…), never here.
hunspell                # the spell-check engine enchant and LibreOffice use
hunspell-en_us          # US English dictionary — the fallback every machine has

# ── version control (always) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The front-end dev toolchain (git-delta, lazygit, github-cli, mise + the Node/LSP
# stack, ripgrep, fd, fzf, bat, cmake, meson) is OPT-IN — see packages/dev.list,
# installed only with `install.sh --dev` (which also runs `mise install`, phase 60).
git                     # VCS — user-facing + the AUR (paru) bootstrap needs it

# ── core GPU userspace (ALWAYS — the whole shell is GPU-accelerated) ──────────
# 64-bit Mesa + the Vulkan loader are mandatory; the per-vendor ICDs/VAAPI are
# added by phase 40. The gaming stack and ALL 32-bit (lib32-*) graphics are
# opt-in — see packages/gaming.list, installed only with `install.sh --gaming`.
mesa
vulkan-icd-loader
vulkan-swrast           # claims the `vulkan-driver` virtual (zed asks for one) before phase 40 adds the real
                        # driver — unclaimed, pacman picked nvidia-utils (1 GB) on Intel and AMD machines too
pciutils                # lspci — GPU/driver introspection (phase 40 'in use: xe' guard)
libva-utils             # vainfo — VAAPI verification (phase 90 postcheck, real HW)
vulkan-tools            # vulkaninfo — Vulkan device verification (phase 90 postcheck)

# ── system tuning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
zram-generator

# ── package tools ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# base-devel (gcc, make, … ~410 MB) is NOT here since 0.44: only an AUR build
# needs it. Komble installs it right before its first AUR build, phase 10 does
# when it has to build paru from source, and everything in aur.list is served
# prebuilt from the [ewe] repo. cmake/meson are in dev.list (--dev).
pacman-contrib          # checkupdates — the only safe update listing (Komble Updates view needs it)
expac                   # fast sync-DB dump — Komble's Browse descriptions come from it
nextcloud-client        # RFC-005/006: nextcloudcmd is the folder-sync engine of the first-party account app (ewe-sync); the client's own GUI is not used
